<title>GREECE: BANK OF CYPRUS EXPANDS FOREIGN CURRENCY LOANS.</title>
<headline>BANK OF CYPRUS EXPANDS FOREIGN CURRENCY LOANS.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Cyprus </p>
<p>introduced new base foreign currency lending rates in French</p>
<p>francs and Italian lire, expanding loan alternatives in foreign</p>
<p>currency, it said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It quoted the following base lending rates in foreign</p>
<p>currency:</p>
<p>    USD    7.25 percent</p>
<p>    GBP    7.25 percent</p>
<p>    DEM    5.00 percent</p>
<p>    ECU    6.00 percent</p>
<p>    JPY    2.50 percent</p>
<p>    ITL   10.00 percent</p>
<p>    FRF    5.50 percent</p>
<p>Bank of Cyprus drachma base lending rates were unchanged as</p>
<p>follows:</p>
<p>    Base lending rate:		     18.75 percent</p>
<p>    Personal/consumer loans:	     23.00 percent</p>
<p>    Renovation loans:			22.00 percent</p>
<p>    Mortgages:				 16.00 percent</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
